{%- doc -%}
  The Black Friday start time (Theme settings > Black Friday > Starts) as unix seconds, or -1 when
  it's blank or can't be read. Shopify's date filter reads "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM" in the shop's
  timezone (Europe/London, clock changes included) and hands the text back unchanged when it
  can't, which is how a bad value is caught (same rule as sections/coszus-promo-banner.liquid).

  @example
  {%- capture bf_start -%}{%- render 'coszus-bf-start' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign raw = settings.bf_start | strip
  assign parsed = raw | date: '%s'
  if raw == blank or parsed == raw
    echo -1
  else
    echo parsed
  endif
-%}
